From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] generate_qmap: drop the QKeyboardMap namespace alias

  webos_keymap_p.h:21:31: error: 'QKeyboardMap' is not a namespace-name
     21 | namespace QEvdevKeyboardMap = QKeyboardMap;

Qt renamed the evdev keymap namespace to QKeyboardMap in 6.9, and upstream
added this alias so webos_keymap[] keeps compiling against Qt's private
QtInputSupport headers.

We do not use those headers here: 0001 makes generate_qmap self-contained by
shipping its own qevdevkeyboard_defaultmap_p.h, which declares
QEvdevKeyboardMap directly for every Qt version. So on Qt 6.12 the alias
refers to a namespace nothing has declared, and the build stops.

generate_qmap.cpp is the only file that includes webos_keymap_p.h, and
nothing else in the tree mentions QKeyboardMap, so the alias can simply go.
This is fallout from 0001 rather than from Qt: the same collision would have
appeared on any Qt >= 6.9.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h b/tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h
index 9dce6b5..4da3c50 100644
--- a/tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h
+++ b/tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h
@@ -17,10 +17,6 @@
 #ifndef WEBOS_KEYMAP_P_H
 #define WEBOS_KEYMAP_P_H
 
-#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(6, 9, 0)
-namespace QEvdevKeyboardMap = QKeyboardMap;
-#endif
-
 // Keymap for WebOS specific
 // { keycode, unicode, qtcode, modifiers, flags, special }
 const QEvdevKeyboardMap::Mapping webos_keymap[] = {
